<title>USA: Harmon Industries sales gain helps Q4 net.</title>
<headline>Harmon Industries sales gain helps Q4 net.</headline>
<dateline>BLUE SPRINGS, Mo. 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Harmon Industries Inc said Tuesday that higher sales helped net income rise by 14 percent in the fourth quarter ended December 31.</p>
<p>The company reported net income of $2.1 million versus $1.8 million one year ago. Sales rose 53 percent to $56 million from $36.5 million, Harmon said.</p>
<p>Harmon said its strength lies in its technological advances in the rail-supply sector.</p>
<p>Harmon markets signal and train control products to railroads and transit systems.</p>
<p>Its shares closed unchanged Tuesday at 18-3/16.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
